{"game": "the-anacrusis", "language": "english", "appid": 1120480, "month": "2025-11", "window": 1, "start_date": 1761955200, "end_date": 1764547199, "month_true_total": 5, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-03 00:45:38 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "210679353", "author": {"steamid": "76561197998501462", "personaname": "Ethosaur", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ethosaur/", "num_games_owned": 750, "num_reviews": 255, "playtime_forever": 101, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 101, "last_played": 1753572761, "avatar": "51334f40526fe0d28fb2b2a87f4f0da23e7cde27"}, "language": "english", "review": "Its alright, and has the \"core\" of what made games like L4D fun, really cool levels, fun artstyle and great workshop support and many interesting weapons/throwables, its fun to play with friends but, sadly the biggest issue for me was that it lacks any real impact and feel when fighting enemies,  especially with some guns feeling and sounding weak, and the swarms animations being kinda \"janky\"\n\nEnemy specials are a bit awkward too at times, especially grabbers and the really bright guys\n\nI say its still worth getting on sale, and the workshop integration and many levels definitely makes it pretty replayable, and thank god for adding a voice wheel, probably my favorite addition in any video game, I love driving my friends crazy with laughs and screams.", "timestamp_created": 1764108741, "timestamp_updated": 1764108741, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.519155323505401611", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "209304973", "author": {"steamid": "76561198109998189", "personaname": "riniort", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "ht